      "role": "user",
      "content": "So if I'm understanding you correctly: the actual volume of suspicious or misleading content hasn't necessarily gone down, we've just changed the way we label it so it doesn't count against our \"misinformation\" targets. \n\nIf I tell the auditors that the \"reduction in misinformation\" is actually just a result of reclassifying high-velocity flags as \"gray area\" content to make the prevalence index look better, they aren't going to see that as a \"refinement.\" They're going to see it as a manipulation of the safety metrics to hide a surge in problematic content. \n\nIs there any actual data to support a decrease in the *raw volume* of unverified claims, or are we strictly looking at a mathematical shift in how those claims are categorized in the final report?",
